{"from": "claim:jn-13-01-supper-before-passover", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-chronology-of-jesus"}
{"from": "claim:jn-13-01-supper-before-passover", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-last-supper"}
{"from": "claim:jn-13-04-05-foot-washing", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-maundy-foot-washing"}
{"from": "claim:jn-13-29-money-box", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-john-13"}
{"from": "claim:jn-13-01-supper-before-passover", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-17-prepare-passover", "note": "Chronology difference: Matthew 26:17 has the disciples prepare the Passover and Matthew presents the supper as that Passover meal; John 13:1 places the supper 'before the feast of the Passover' (and 18:28 keeps the leaders from the praetorium so they may eat the Passover). John's last meal is not the seder."}
{"from": "claim:jn-13-01-supper-before-passover", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-14-12-sacrificed-passover", "note": "Chronology difference: Mark 14:12 dates the meal on the day 'when they sacrificed the Passover' lambs; John 13:1 dates the supper before the feast of the Passover, so the crucifixion falls on 14 Nisan in John."}
{"from": "claim:jn-13-27-satan-entered-judas", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:lk-22-03-satan-entered-judas", "note": "Timing difference: Luke places 'Satan entered into Judas' before the betrayal bargain; John 13:2 says the devil had already put it into his heart before supper and 13:27 places the entry after the dipped morsel."}
{"from": "claim:jn-13-04-05-foot-washing", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:1-samuel-25-41", "note": "Cross-reference, not evidence: Abigail says 'Behold, your servant is a servant to wash the feet of the servants of my lord' - foot washing as a servant's task in the Hebrew Bible; also Genesis 18:4 and 19:2 (hosts offer water for feet) and Luke 7:44 (a host gives water for the feet)."}
{"from": "claim:jn-13-04-05-foot-washing", "type": "related_to", "to": "passage:lk-07-44", "note": "Cross-reference: Luke 7:44 'You gave me no water for my feet' presupposes the same host-provides-foot-water custom of the period; a Gospel cross-reference, not independent evidence."}
{"from": "claim:jn-13-18-psalm-41-9-quoted", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:psalm-41-9", "note": "Cross-reference, not evidence: Psalm 41:9 'my own familiar friend, who ate bread with me, has lifted up his heel against me'; the WEB New Testament renders the quotation 'He who eats bread with me has lifted up his heel against me'."}
{"from": "claim:jn-13-29-money-box", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:2-chronicles-24-8-11", "note": "Cross-reference, not evidence: the same word glōssokomon names the chest for collecting Temple money in 2 Chronicles 24:8,11 (Septuagint), per the fetched Wikipedia John 13 article; a portable chest for money, not the disciples' box itself."}
{"from": "passage:jn-13-21", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-26-21"}
{"from": "passage:jn-13-21", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mk-14-18"}
{"from": "passage:jn-13-21", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:lk-22-21", "note": "Luke says the hand of the betrayer is 'with me on the table'; John names the dipped morsel as the sign."}
{"from": "passage:jn-13-26", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-26-23", "note": "Matthew has the betrayer dip his hand with Jesus in the dish; John has Jesus himself dip the morsel and give it to Judas."}
{"from": "passage:jn-13-26", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mk-14-20", "note": "Mark has the betrayer dip with Jesus in the dish; John has Jesus dip the morsel and hand it to Judas."}
{"from": "passage:jn-13-27", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:lk-22-03", "note": "Both tell of Satan and Judas; Luke places the entry before the bargain, John after the morsel at supper (see the claims' related_to note)."}
{"from": "passage:jn-13-38", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-26-34"}
{"from": "passage:jn-13-38", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mk-14-30", "note": "Mark has the rooster crow twice; John agrees with Matthew's single crow before the three denials."}
{"from": "passage:jn-13-38", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:lk-22-34"}
