{"from": "claim:jn-13-04-05-foot-washing", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:lk-22-24-27-greatness-dispute", "note": "Narrative difference at the same meal: Luke has a dispute about who was greatest, answered with 'I am among you as one who serves'; John tells no dispute but the foot washing itself, with the same maxim 'a servant is not greater than his lord' (13:16)."}
{"from": "claim:jn-13-23-25-beloved-disciple-reclining", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-20-reclining-twelve", "note": "Both Gospels place the meal reclining; John adds the beloved disciple's place at Jesus's breast (a guest's position of honor) and, in John's chronology, dates the meal before Passover, where Matthew calls it the Passover meal."}
